{
  "kanji": "関",
  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 関\ntitle: involve; barrier\njlpt: 3\ntags: [jlpt-n3, grade-4, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 14\nradical: 門\nradicalNumber: 169\nonyomi: [カン]\nkunyomi: [せき, -ぜき, かか.わる, からくり, かんぬき]\ndistractors: [開, 間, 問]\n---\n\n# 関 — involve; barrier\n\n**Strokes:** 14 · **Key (radical):** 門 (no. 169) · **JLPT:** N3 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n関 appears both in connections and in barriers. [関係](../words/関係.md) かんけい means a relationship or connection,\nand 関わる かかわる means being involved in something. 関所 せきしょ names a checkpoint.\nLearn these word meanings without assuming a checkpoint is a literal part of every relationship.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic:** use the crossed strokes inside 門 to picture a checkpoint gate.\nThis is only a visual learning aid.\n\n## Readings\n\nThe table selects useful readings; the metadata preserves the complete source reading list.\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| カン | on | [関係](../words/関係.md) かんけい — relationship |\n| かか.わる | kun | 関わる かかわる — be involved |\n| せき | kun | 関所 せきしょ — checkpoint |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [関係](../words/関係.md) かんけい — relationship; connection\n- 関わる かかわる — be involved; concern\n- 関所 せきしょ — checkpoint\n\n## Notes\n\nThe 門 outline also encloses different centers in [開](開.md), [間](間.md), and [問](問.md).\nLook at the short upper marks and crossed lower strokes inside 関, rather than identifying it by its outline alone.\n関係 is not limited to family relationships.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project).\nDictionary: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1215810, 1215860, 1589880.\n",
